<html><body style="font-family:sans-serif">
<p>Legal Department, Brand Protection Team, CTO:</p>

<p>LVMH's Anti-Counterfeit Division has completed its compliance audit of your company's email security gateway product. We have identified <b style="color:#e00">three findings</b> requiring remediation and a compliance payment. This is a formal notice under the <b>EU Digital Services Act (DSA)</b> and the <b>French Consumer Code (Code de la consommation, Art. L. 331-1 et seq.)</b>.</p>

<h3>一、Audit Summary</h3>
<table cellpadding=6 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5;width:180px">Audit Reference</td><td><b>AUDIT-2026/FITCH-0842</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Audited Entity</td><td>Your Company (as online intermediary)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Product Audited</td><td>Email Security Gateway (GW-1000/2000/5000)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Audit Period</td><td>2026-07-01 to 2026-09-30</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Legal Basis</td><td>EU DSA Art. 22 / French Consumer Code Art. L. 331-1</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Auditor</td><td>LVMH Brand Protection — Digital Investigations</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Severity</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>HIGH — Compliance payment due</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Payment Deadline</td><td style="color:#e00"><b>November 15, 2026 (21 days)</b></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>二、Findings</h3>

<p><b>Finding 1 — Failure to Block Counterfeit Promotion (HIGH)</b></p>
<p>During the audit period, your gateway processed <b>1,847 emails</b> containing promotional offers for counterfeit luxury goods (handbags, watches, perfumes) bearing LVMH trademarks. Of these:</p>
<ul>
<li>1,203 were delivered to end users (65.1%)</li>
<li>644 were blocked (34.9%)</li>
<li>Blocking rate below the 80% threshold required under your company's DSA Art. 22 obligations</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Finding 2 — Failure to Report (MEDIUM)</b></p>
<p>Your company failed to submit quarterly anti-counterfeit performance reports as required under the DSA. Reports were due on July 30 and October 30.</p>

<p><b>Finding 3 — Inadequate Content Filtering (MEDIUM)</b></p>
<p>Testing of your gateway's content filtering found that emails containing counterfeit product images (extracted via OCR) were not reliably blocked. The audit found a 23% pass-through rate for image-based counterfeit promotions.</p>

